Just how much farming does one need to do to get +60 worth of IA rings? 
If we're going to consider farming-reliant strategies, it becomes 
pointless to discuss anything else, given that a sufficiently farmed 
character only needs one item (a source of MR).

Anyway, the -20 penalty doesn't require much effort to offset:

+30 for levels (a couple cursed magic markers, plus conflict in the 
Valley)
+13 for luck (easy)
+4 for 18 dex
+5 more if you bother with dex gloves
+2 for a reasonably high strength, or +3 for 18/**
+7 for a highly enchanted weapon
+d5 for most artifacts
-4 if you haven't managed to get to Basic in the weapon

And we're already well past the amount needed (+31) to always hit a 
disenchanter's -10AC.  Player monsters on Astral will have better ACs, 
but one shouldn't melee those. 



